# Forge build program

Canonical copies: `docs/spec-references/`. Read them before any Forge build. Do not implement a layer until the user feeds that build prompt.

## Which doc wins

All paths are under `docs/spec-references/`. Call them by the filename in `INDEX-and-feed-list.md`.

1. `spec-reconciliation-overlay.md` — current repo vs target. Wins on conflict.
2. Tier 2 specs — target contracts for the layer being built (table below).
3. `cinematic-forge-architecture.md` — spine, stages, pool, chokepoints.
4. `INDEX-and-feed-list.md` — document map and feed order with gates.
5. `SPEC-00-INDEX-and-conventions.md` through `SPEC-10-llm-intelligence.md` — per-control contracts. Read the matching file when changing that system. Overlay still wins.
6. `BP-00-INDEX-and-rules.md` — the execution queue for those control specs (BP-01 through BP-13). Feed one BP per session, only after the user feeds that prompt. It does not replace build-0 through build-6.
7. `TR-00-INDEX.md` — Training Studio (TR-01 through TR-06). After MP-01..12. Feed one TR per session, only after the user feeds that prompt. Overlay still wins. It does not lift `GENERATION_PAUSED`.
8. `WF-00-INDEX.md` — Workflow parity (WF-01 through WF-03). Phase 2 after MP + OR + moat demo. Feed one WF per session, only after the user feeds that prompt. Overlay still wins. It does not lift `GENERATION_PAUSED`.

When a layer finishes, its overlay correction becomes true.

