## Feed order (do not skip a gate)

Keep `GENERATION_PAUSED=true` until Gate 0 passes. No billable generation except the single confirm shot a gate explicitly allows.

0. Safety (build-0) — Gate 0: every paid call through `submitToFal` / `providerSubmit` and `claudeCall`; eval harness cannot auto-run; CI grep; 15 min zero dashboard calls; then one manual shot.
1. Unify stores (build-1) — Gate 1: one timeline store; a Simple shot appears in Ultimate.
2. Shared core `@cinema/core` (build-2) — raised by the overlay. Defer only if the user explicitly chooses momentum over maintainability. Revert any step that breaks web.
3. Generation patches (build-3) — Gate 3: Veo silent, registry ids match real endpoints, named play() error guards.
4. Character / location (build-4) — Gate 4: 3-shot face consistency + a located shot.
5. Moat + audio (build-5) — audio (Part B) before cognition wiring (Part A).
6. Pro tools (build-6) — per tool, not one gate.

Minimum demo = Gates 0, 1, 3, 4 + build-5 Part B.

## Already done — do not rebuild

`resolveModel` throws (no model swap). `dispatch.ts` provider switch. OpenAPI payload clamp. Kling/PixVerse audio-off. `reconcileTimeline` maps `videoUrl` → `sourceUrl`. `addClip` rejects missing `sourceUrl`. R2 mirror on completion. `canPlaySrc`. Auth tables + additive migrations only (never reset).

## Name map

Spec Shot = `StudioClip`. Spec Character = `VaultCharacter`. Spec Clip = timeline clip. `videoUrl` matches. Add spec columns only when the active layer needs them (`falRequestId`, `characterIds`, `locationId`, seed, `voiceId` on the character).
